---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Invitation from '../components/Invitation.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Personal AI setup & support"
  description="Hands-on help setting up AI agents around your own workload. Work with Alastair Brayne on admin, context, planning and workflows you can keep using."
  service="Personal AI agent setup and support"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap interior-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow red">Personal AI support</p><h1>
          You know AI could help.<br />Let’s get it working<br />for you.
        </h1><p class="lead">
          The admin, the follow-ups, the workstream you keep meaning to sort out. Start with
          something that matters in your day, and get hands-on help putting an agent to work.
        </p><a class="button" href="/enquire/?need=personal"
          >Talk about your workload <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div><div class="personal-paper" aria-hidden="true">
        <p>Still on your mind?</p><ul>
          <li>The inbox</li><li>The follow-ups</li><li>That half-finished plan</li>
        </ul><span>Let’s start with one.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap reading-layout section">
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <p>On this page</p><a href="#starting">Start with your day</a><a href="#setup"
        >What we set up</a
      ><a href="#fit">Who it’s for</a><a href="#questions">Practical questions</a>
    </nav><div class="prose">
      <section id="starting">
        <h2>You don’t need another list of things AI can do.</h2><p class="lead">
          You need help making it useful for the way you actually work.
        </p><p>
          You might have tried a few tools, had some impressive conversations, and still find the
          same jobs waiting for you. Or you may know where you want help but not how to connect the
          pieces.
        </p><p>
          We choose a real workstream and work through it together. You get practical setup, an
          explanation of what is happening, and conventions you can return to once the session is
          over.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="setup">
        <h2>Give your agent some context.</h2><p>
          A useful agent needs to understand your work. We can set up a library of context, reusable
          skills, and sensible ways to store and update information. Claude is one tool I work with;
          the setup depends on what you need and already use.
        </p><h3>A place to begin</h3><p>
          That could be organising information for a recurring project, preparing for meetings,
          drafting follow-ups, or helping triage email. We look at what the agent needs access to,
          where you want to stay involved, and which actions should wait for your approval.
        </p><h3>A setup you understand</h3><p>
          We work together so you can see how the pieces fit. You learn how to give useful
          direction, recognise when an answer needs checking, and adjust the setup as your work
          changes.
        </p><h3>Conventions that make it easier to return</h3><p>
          Clear places for context, ongoing tasks and reusable instructions reduce the effort of
          starting again. Where scheduled tasks are useful, we agree what they should do and how you
          will know whether they worked.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="fit">
        <h2>For a busy mind, and a real workload.</h2><p>
          I work with business owners, leaders, coaches and people managing their own work. You do
          not need to be a developer. Curiosity and a willingness to try things are a useful
          starting point.
        </p><p>
          Executive function is one of the meanings behind ExFu. I’m interested in making these
          tools helpful for people with ADHD and other neurodivergent ways of working. We can
          account for how you plan, maintain context and return to a task, without expecting you to
          become a different person.
        </p><p>
          This is practical AI consultancy. My psychotherapy training informs how I work with
          people; these sessions are not therapy or clinical care.
        </p><p>
          If you are setting this up as a leader, your own experience can also become a useful
          foundation for deciding how to <a href="/fractional-support/"
            >bring AI into the wider business</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <section class="section faq-section" id="questions">
    <div class="wrap reading-layout">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Before we start</p><h2>A practical<br />conversation.</h2></div><div
        class="faqs"
      >
        <details open>
          <summary>Do I need to know which tool I want?</summary><p>
            No. Tell me what you would like help with and what you already use. We can work out a
            sensible starting point together.
          </p>
        </details><details>
          <summary>Will I need a paid AI subscription?</summary><p>
            Some setups need paid tools. We discuss that before agreeing the work, so you understand
            the separate costs and what access is needed.
          </p>
        </details><details>
          <summary>Is this a course or one-to-one help?</summary><p>
            This offer is hands-on, one-to-one support around your own work. We agree the scope and
            format in conversation.
          </p>
        </details><details>
          <summary>Can we do this remotely?</summary><p>
            Yes. We can work together remotely. Bristol sessions may also be possible by
            arrangement.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Invitation title="What would you like to get on top of?" />
</Layout>
